  "interpretation_limits": [
    "The factor-combination intervention is an artificial, retrospectively motivated change to reproductive pairing laws; source Model3 original biology remains unchanged.",
    "Upper bound P=3^m is a potential combinatorial genotype count given surviving alleles, NOT proof of one-step biological accessibility or actual diversity.",
    "Coverage rises partly because its denominator falls as allele types disappear; coverage increase is NOT direct evidence of active adaptive compensation.",
    "Stable class richness with declining Shannon and Simpson effective richness is consistent with increased genotype-frequency concentration. Magnitudes are conditional on fixed K32 old visitor history and engineered genetic founders.",
    "The log richness = log combinatorial upper bound + log coverage identity holds exactly per living population, with occupancy-weighted version reported for factorial contrasts. It is an algebraic identity, not causal mechanism identification.",
